    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211">

                <pb facs="0701" n="687" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg687"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Clayton, Secretary
                        of State, to Mr. Hall, district
                        attorney.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1849-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >September</hi> 19, 1849</date>.</dateline>
                <p><seg type="margin">[657]</seg> *<hi rendition="#small-caps">J. Prescott
                    Hall</hi>, Esq.,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">United States District Attorney for
                        the Southern District of New York</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In acknowledging the receipt of your letter
                    of the 15th instant, it is due to you to say, that the President highly approves
                    of the prompt, energetic, and judicious manner in which you have executed all
                    the instructions of this Department, touching the late attempt on the part of
                    some of our misguided citizens, who were concerned in a mischievous and illegal
                    project for the invasion of the island of Cuba. To this expression from the
                    President I have great pleasure in adding this Department’s unqualified
                    approbation of your official conduct.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, with great respect, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOHN M. CLAYTON.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
